{"id":"word:hebrew:H6828","type":"word","title":"צָפוֹן","subtitle":"H6828 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, hidden , i.e. dark ; used only of the north as a quarter (gloomy and unknown)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to צָפוֹן (H6828) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-f.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 153 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"צָפוֹן (tsâphôwn) means properly, hidden , i.e. dark ; used only of the north as a quarter (gloomy and unknown) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 9 24."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"צָפוֹן","transliteration":"tsâphôwn","pronunciation":"tsaw-fone'","strong":"H6828","lemmaId":"hebrew:H6828","partOfSpeech":"n-f","forms":["הַ/צָּפ֔וֹן","צָפ֑וֹן","צָפ֔וֹן","צָפֽוֹן","צָפ֑וֹנָ/ה"],"morphs":[["HNcfsa/Sd",43],["HNcfsa",38],["HR/Ncfsa",24],["HTd/Ncfsa",22],["HR/Ncfsc",8],["HC/Ncfsa/Sd",5],["HRd/Ncfsa",4],["HC/R/Ncfsa",2],["HTd/Ncfsa/Sd",2],["HR/Ncfsa/Sd",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, hidden , i.e. dark ; used only of the north as a quarter (gloomy and unknown)","usage":"north(-ern, side, -ward, wind).","full":"H6828. tsaphon I. צָפוֺן 153 noun feminine Isa 43:6 north (as the hidden, dark ; compare Thes Lewy Fremdw. 188 f. ; perhaps Phoenician צפל north ); — absolute ׳צ Jeremiah 26:26 +, צָפֹ֫נָה northward Gen 13:14 +, oftener צָפ֫וֺנָה Jer 3:12 +, also צָפ֫וֺנָה = צָפוֺן 1:13 + (after prepositions and stative construct; compare Ges § 90e ); construct לְ מִצְּפוֺן Josh 8:11 +, also מִצְּפוֺן 19:14 Gi (compare Benn; van d. H. Baer ׳מִצָּ ), לְ מִצְּפ֫וֺנָה Judg 21:19 ; ( ׳צ occurs oftenest in Ezekiel [46 t.], Joshua [25 t.], Jeremiah [25 t.], Daniel [9 t.]); — north (opposite south, east, west) Gen 13:14 ; 28:14 (both J), Exod 27:11 (P), +; צ ׳מְּאַת north side 26:20 ; Josh 15:5 + (see מֵּאָה ); so צ ׳צֶלַיע Exod 26:35 , הַצּ ׳רוּחַ Ezek 42:17 , compare צָפ֫וֺנָה הַמִּזְבֵּחַ עַליֶֿרֶךְ 2Kin 16:14 ; צ ׳גְּבוּל Num 34:7 , 9 north boundary ; צ ׳יַתְכְּתֵי remote parts of north Isa 14:13 (as divine abode), Ezek 38:6 , 15 + (see [ יַרְכָה ]); הַצּ ׳שַׁעַר 40:35 +, צ ׳מֶּתַח 42:2 ; צ ׳רוּחַ Ezekiel 25:23 north wind , and so ׳צ alone Song 4:16 ; toward the north is צָפ֫וֺנָה Josh 13:3 +? אֶלצָֿפוֺן Eccl 1:6 , ׳אֶלהַֿצּ Ezek 42:1 , אֶלהַֿצָּפ֫וֺנָה 8:14 , לַצָּפוֺן 40:23 , הַצָּפוֺן דֶּרֶךְ 40:20 , ׳ד צָפ֫וֺנָה 8:5 (twice in verse) +, etc.; especially (in Jeremiah, Ezekiel, etc.) of quarter whence invaders were to come, e. g. Assyrians Isa 14:31 , compare Zeph 2:13 , Babylonians Jer 6:1 , 22 ; 15:12 ; 46:20 , 24 ( ׳עַםצֿ ), 47:2 , Ezek 26:7 , Cyrus against Babylonian Isa 41:25 , compare Jer 50:3 , 9 , 41 ; 51:48 ; more vaguely, 1:14-15 , ( צ ׳מַמְלְכוֺת ), 4:6 ; 10:22 ; 13:20 ; 25:9 , 26 ( הַצּ ׳מַלְכֵי ); of Gog's host Ezek 38:6 , 15 ; 39:2 ; צ ׳נְסִיכֵי 32:30 (apparently of nearer [Aramaean?] princes); צ ׳אֶרֶץ Jer 31:8 is region of Carchemish, but Zech 2:10 ; 6:6 , 8 (twice in verse) of Babylon; צ ׳מֵאֶרֶץ (sometimes + other countries) the exiles and dispersed are to return Jer 3:18 ; 16:15 = 23:8 ; 31:8 , compare Isa 43:6 ; 49:12 ; הַצּ ׳מֶלֶךְ Dan 11:6-7 , 8 , 11 , 13 , 15 , 40 denotes successive Seleucidae.","rootNote":"or צָפֹן ; from 6845 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 9 24","keyReferences":["1Chr 9 24","1Chr 26 14","1Chr 26 17","1Kgs 7 25","1Sam 14 5","2Chr 4 4","2Kgs 16 14","Amos 8 12"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":153,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 9 24","book":"1Chr","chapter":9,"verse":24,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"צָפ֥וֹנָ/ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsa/Sd"},{"reference":"1Chr 26 14","book":"1Chr","chapter":26,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"צָפֽוֹנָ/ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsa/Sd"},{"reference":"1Chr 26 17","book":"1Chr","chapter":26,"verse":17,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לַ/צָּפ֤וֹנָ/ה","